ure is\n   150\tcontent-hashed and migrates every downstream consumer, and duplicates\n   151\tauthority over a fact a query could derive fresh instead. This is not a\n   152\tzero-cost trade — deriving still costs real query complexity and, if the\n   153\tfact isn't already indexed, the work of building and maintaining whatever\n   154\tdoes index it — but that cost is paid once, in the query and its index,\n   155\tnot in every future migration of the persisted structure. See\n   156\t[`docs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md`](./yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md)'s\n   157\tretired `:global` tag for the concrete case study — a free/bound variable\n   158\tdistinction that looked like it needed a new AST node, until it turned\n   159\tout to be computable by query; getting the scope right there took two\n   160\trounds and a real correctness bug (a query that looked sufficient\n   161\tundercounted a dependency in a case the simpler query didn't cover).\n   162\t\n   163\tSee [`docs/agents/malleability.md`](../agents/malleability.md) for complete design guidance (cohesion, coupling, bounded complexity, evolution, testing strategy).\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
