{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"agent_message","text":"## Verdict: **No — not safe to commit as-is**\n\nI read both files in full. Most fixes landed, but one r1 finding remains unchanged and two replacements introduce inaccurate claims.\n\n### Eight-item verification\n\n| # | Result | Assessment |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1 | **FAIL** | AST extraction now uses root-scoped occurrences. Segment extraction is labeled unverified, but its explanation incorrectly says `linearize/lower` does not exist. |\n| 2 | **PASS** | Historical no-fallthrough behavior correctly says “evaluating an unbound name to nil” at [675](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md:675). |\n| 3 | **FAIL** | All four stale blocking statements were replaced, but the new §4.4 paragraph overstates encoder guarantees and repeats the wrong conformance pair. |\n| 4 | **PASS** | §10 correctly names vector/list and vector/seq, explicitly preserving list/seq equality at [1987–1990](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md:1987). |\n| 5 | **PASS, with wording correction below** | [736–748](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md:736) clearly distinguishes single-root test correctness from production root-scoping requirements. |\n| 6 | **PASS** | [691–700](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md:691) accurately identifies the fixture-specific edge clauses and missing grammar coverage. |\n| 7 | **PASS** | [585–592](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md:585) now identifies ambient print bindings as a present concern. |\n| 8 | **PASS** | [datom.world.md:141–161](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/datom.world.md:141) requires correct scope and acknowledges query/indexing costs. |\n\n### Remaining corrections\n\n1. **The unchanged r1 resolution finding still blocks approval.**  \n   [Line 1163](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md:1163) still says §7.4 checks variable nesting and an unbound runtime `:var` evaluates to `nil`. The scope check was removed; retained resolution falls through and throws when unresolved ([engine.cljc:46–65](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc:46)). Missing parameters explicitly bound to nil are different.\n\n2. **The replacement sharing paragraph needs two corrections.**  \n   [Line 633](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md:633):\n   - Still lists **seq/list**, rather than **vector/seq**.\n   - Claims unconditional injectivity over “ordinary values,” omitting the live ambient-print caveat now acknowledged in §4.2. With `*print-readably*` false, ordinary string `\"x\"` and symbol `x` both print as `x`; scalar printing still delegates to `pr-str`. Qualify the sharing guarantee by the supported encoding conditions.\n\n3. **Distinguish existing lowering from the proposed replacement.**  \n   [Lines 1239–1240](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md:1239) say `linearize.cljc`’s `lower` is unimplemented. It exists at [linearize.cljc:162](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/linearize.cljc:162), taking AST datoms. Say the proposed **row-set-to-vector lowering** and segment free-name query remain unverified.\n\n4. **Do not attribute full-grammar coverage to the fixture test.**  \n   [Lines 749–753](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md:749) say the test proves correctness across the whole grammar. The test demonstrates one single-root application/lambda case. Generality follows from the path-based algorithm, assuming complete occurrence data; label that as reasoning, not tested coverage.\n\nThe root-scoping correction **does not conflict with approving the test within its single-root scope**. All seven `:global` hits remain confined to the historical discussion in §4.5.\n\nNo files were edited; tests were inspected, not executed."}}
